# File: specs/362-make-completed-delivery-re-entry-idempotent-after-branch-restoration/feature.gherkin
Feature: Make completed delivery re-entry idempotent after branch restoration
  A delivery that already merged and closed its issue must remain successful
  when its worker invokes delivery again from the restored default branch.

  @SCN001 @regression
  Scenario: Completed re-entry succeeds without local verification files
    Given persisted delivery is complete for an exact pull request and head
    And the restored default branch lacks the issue verification report
    When delivery is invoked again
    Then it validates the remote merged pull request and closed issue
    And it writes a passed delivery handoff and exits zero

  @SCN002 @regression
  Scenario: Completed re-entry performs no mutations
    Given terminal remote proof matches persisted delivery identity
    When completed delivery re-entry runs
    Then it performs no git or GitHub mutation

  @SCN003 @regression
  Scenario: Terminal identity mismatch fails closed
    Given terminal remote proof does not match the persisted pull request, head, merged state, or issue closure
    When completed delivery re-entry runs
    Then it fails with the existing reconciliation or merge-proof classification
    And it does not report success

  @SCN004 @regression
  Scenario: Owned smoke observes successful execute completion
    Given an owned smoke delivery merged its exact pull request and closed its issue
    When its delivery worker repeats delivery before settlement
    Then execute exits zero with invocation-owned delivery proof
